@title INC-3107 Postmortem
@subtitle EU matchmaking DNS misconfiguration, Alder Cloud Games
@author Network team
@date 2026-08-19

kpi Duration | 1 h 52 min | | bad
kpi Lowest success rate | 61.3% | | bad
kpi Matches failed | 48,200
kpi Region | EU-West

## What happened
A Terraform change replaced the weighted DNS records for `match.eu` with a single record pointing at a decommissioned load balancer, so players in Europe could not reach matchmaking. The record was restored at 10:11, but resolvers had cached the failed lookups with a negative-cache TTL of 3600 seconds, which kept failures going for nearly an hour after the fix.

## Timeline
table = Time (UTC),Event; 09:12,Terraform apply; 09:15,Success rate drops; 09:31,Player reports spike on social media; 09:40,Incident declared; 10:05,Bad record identified; 10:11,Record restored; 11:04,Success rate back above 99% and incident resolved

